{"seed_id": "BigCodeBench/7", "verdict": "update", "note": "", "author": "author_2", "prompt": "Write a program that reads sales records from standard input and prints the name of the best-selling product.\n\nInput format:\n- The first line is a header line (its content can be ignored).\n- Each subsequent line contains a product record with exactly two comma-separated fields: the product name (a string, which may contain spaces but not commas and escape sequence) and the quantity sold (an integer), e.g. \"Product B,200\".\n- Input ends at end-of-file.\n\nBehavior:\n- For each product name, sum the quantities from all of its rows to get its total quantity sold.\n- Determine the product with the largest total quantity. If several products tie for the largest total, choose whichever of them was the first to reach that maximum total quantity while scanning the rows in the order they appear in the input.\n- Print that product's name exactly as it appears in the input, on a single line, with no extra text.\n- If there are no data rows after the header, or if any quantity field cannot be parsed as an integer, print exactly the single word \"Error\" and nothing else.\n\nExample:\nInput:\n```\nproduct,quantity\nProduct B,200\nProduct A,100\n```\nOutput:\n```\nProduct B\n```"}
