{"seed_id": "BigCodeBench/329", "verdict": "update", "note": "Prompt doesn't say what happens when '(' has no matching ')' later in the text (tested by the \"unclosed text continues\" case); gold takes the rest of the string as one token.", "author": "author_2", "prompt": "Write a program that reads two things from standard input:\n1. The first line contains a file name (a plain string, with no path separators).\n2. All remaining lines contain the literal text of a JSON object. The JSON object's values are all strings (the object itself has no nested structures).\n\nBuild a single text string by taking the JSON object's string values, in the order they appear in the object, and joining them with a single space.\n\nFrom that combined text, produce a list of tokens according to these rules, scanning the text left to right:\n- Whenever you encounter an opening parenthesis '(', treat everything from that '(' up to and including the very next ')' as one single token (this token includes both parentheses and everything in between).\n- If an opening parenthesis '(' has no closing ')' anywhere later in the text, its token instead consists of that '(' together with all remaining characters through the end of the text.\n- Any character that is a letter, digit, or underscore that is NOT inside such a parenthesized span is its own individual token.\n- All other characters (spaces, punctuation, etc.) that are not inside a parenthesized span and are not letters/digits/underscore are ignored and produce no token.\n\nCollect the tokens in the order they occur in the combined text.\n\nFinally, print a JSON object (using standard JSON formatting with double quotes) that has exactly one key equal to the file name read from the first input line, whose value is the list of tokens (as JSON strings) in the order collected. Print nothing else.\n\nExample:\nInput:\n```\nsample_data.json\n{\"content\": \"This is a (sample) text with some (matches) and characters.\"}\n```\nOutput:\n```\n{\"sample_data.json\": [\"T\", \"h\", \"i\", \"s\", \"i\", \"s\", \"a\", \"(sample)\", \"t\", \"e\", \"x\", \"t\", \"w\", \"i\", \"t\", \"h\", \"s\", \"o\", \"m\", \"e\", \"(matches)\", \"a\", \"n\", \"d\", \"c\", \"h\", \"a\", \"r\", \"a\", \"c\", \"t\", \"e\", \"r\", \"s\"]}\n```"}
